# Thread 3 — move verification uses a post-push re-read; ticket E4 prescribes the push's own sha

**Status: fixed per E4** — the record now verifies against the **push's own sha**, with the re-read demoted to a fallback.

- `silentUpdateBranch` / `forkSilentUpdateBranch` (and the gh-1106 escalation success path) return the pushed sha: right after the push chain succeeds, `pushedHeadShaOf(dir)` runs `git -C <attempt-dir> rev-parse HEAD` in the attempt's own checkout — locally computed, zero API reads, lag-immune. The command builder itself is untouched (the gh-1074 byte-identical chain pins stay green); only a trailing local probe was added.
- `refreshHeadSilent` uses it first and falls back to the fresh `github_get_pr` read only when the local probe has no answer (mocks, executor limits) — the E1 surface is unchanged:

```js
newHeadMtt = (typeof pushedShaMtt === 'string' && pushedShaMtt)
    ? pushedShaMtt
    : freshHeadSha(effectiveRepoInfo, ticket.prNumber);
```

TDD: a new E4 test (`js/unit-tests/test_smAgent.js`, movedThisTick suite) simulates the live 2026-10-19 16:43 lag — the re-read answers the **pre-push** sha while the checkout's `rev-parse` knows the new one. Pre-fix the move was silently swallowed (no deferral, the superseded head reached the verdict — exactly the fail-open the thread describes); post-fix the record comes from the push itself and the verdict is deferred.

